  "body": "## Changes\n\n- Terminal tabs now show available conversation titles. Rename individual\n  terminals from their context menus or the command palette, and reset them to\n  automatic naming at any time. An optional rename shortcut is available in Hotkeys.\n- Manual task names persist across reconnection and relaunch. Settings \u2192 Terminal\n  lets you keep them until reset or clear them when a different known agent\n  conversation starts. Automatic titles omit matching project-directory suffixes.\n- Refined workspace styling with a rounded frame, balanced Tabs-mode insets and\n  smaller, muted space headings.\n- Improved terminal ownership across backend pane remapping.\n- Fixed stale mouse capture after a foreground TUI returns control to its shell,\n  including sessions that were detached or handed off to a replacement backend.\n\n## Downloads and known limits\n\n- macOS: Apple silicon. The app is ad-hoc signed and not notarized.\n- Linux: x86_64 and ARM64 tarballs and Debian packages, built on Ubuntu 24.04.\n  X11/XWayland, Vulkan, GTK 3 and WebKitGTK 4.1 are required. Arch binary packages\n  target x86_64; AUR publication remains deferred.\n- Automatic titles and conversation-based name reset depend on agent metadata.\n  Repeated identical titles after a conversation change may use the process fallback.\n- Mouse recovery requires the backend to observe the return to the shell. It does\n  not restore terminated processes, extended keyboard modes or shell terminal settings.\n- Agent notifications remain best effort. Task names are not included in notifications.\n- Verification used automated UI/model tests, isolated real terminal sessions and\n  package checks. Native desktop/banner interaction and v0.3.2 upgrade testing were\n  not performed for this release candidate.\n- External native plugin payloads are distributed separately.\n\n[Full changelog](https://github.com/rengwu/chartr/compare/v0.3.2...v0.3.3)\n"
